    "title": "$1.5 million lottery ticket winner sold in Indiana - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ohio Statewide Staff ,\n2 hours ago INDIANA — A lottery player on the southwest side of Indianapolis is holding a ticket worth more than $1.5 million following Tuesday night’s CA$H 5 drawing. According to the Hoosier Lottery, a winning CA$H 5 ticket worth $1,571,745 was sold at Hoosier to Go, located at 5220 West Troy Avenue. The ticket matched all five winning numbers drawn on Tuesday, June 16. Read full article\n9",
